$post=(Hero 'AI content · 8 min read' 'A practical guide to AI content automation' 'How to increase output while preserving quality, oversight, and a recognizable voice.')+"<article class=`"section`"><div class=`"container prose`"><p>AI content automation works best as a system, not a single prompt. Strong workflows connect a clear brief, trusted source material, generation, human review, publishing, and measurement.</p><h2>Start with the bottleneck</h2><p>Map the current process and identify the slowest repeatable step: research, scripting, resizing, captions, or scheduling.</p><h2>Design for review</h2><p>Automation should make judgment easier. Add approval stages for claims, brand-sensitive language, and final creative decisions.</p><h2>Build a simple pipeline</h2><ol><li>Capture ideas in one structured location.</li><li>Enrich ideas with audience and campaign context.</li><li>Generate a draft in a consistent format.</li><li>Route it to a human reviewer.</li><li>Publish approved assets and collect results.</li></ol><h2>Measure and maintain</h2><p>Track time saved, approval rate, output consistency, audience retention, and business outcomes. Document who owns integrations, exceptions, and changes.</p><div class=`"cta-band`"><h2>Want help designing your content engine?</h2><a class=`"btn btn-primary`" href=`"/contact.html`">Talk to Us</a></div></div></article>"
